{"qid":"Q36","names":["Republic of Poland"],"title":"Republic of Poland","endonym":{"native":"Polska","lang":"pl"},"capsule":"The Polish People's Republic, renamed the Republic of Poland (Rzeczpospolita Polska) in December 1989 following the Solidarity-led democratic transition, is a Central European state whose post-1945 borders were redrawn westward to the Oder–Neisse line at Potsdam, incorporating former German territories while losing the Kresy regions to the Soviet Union. Poland joined NATO in 1999 and the European Union in 2004, marking its full reintegration into Western institutions after decades of communist rule. The country's population of approximately 38 million makes it the sixth most populous EU member state, with Warsaw as its capital and economic center.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern borders are precisely defined by international treaty and cartographic survey; the post-1945 western boundary was confirmed definitively by the Treaty on the Final Settlement with Respect to Germany (1990).","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Poland","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poland"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Poland (1989–present)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Poland_(1989%E2%80%93present)"}],"britannica":"place/Poland","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Poland","rulers":[{"qid":"Q55832","name":"Bolesław Bierut","start":1952,"end":1954,"image":"PL Bolesław Bierut (1892-1956).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/PL%20Boles%C5%82aw%20Bierut%20(1892-1956).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Burzyńs